{"extract": "Colin Berkeley Moynihan, 4th Baron Moynihan, 4th Baronet (born 13 September 1955), is a British Olympic silver medalist, politician, businessman and sports administrator. Lord Moynihan served as the Chairman of the British Olympic Association (BOA) from 2005 to 2012. A member of the Conservative Party, he was as a Member of Parliament (MP) representing the constituency of Lewisham East from 1983 to 1992, and was the Minister for Sport from 1987 to 1990. He became a member of the House of Lords in 1997.", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "1978 FISA Lightweight Championships", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "1981 World Rowing Championships", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "1999 House of Lords elections", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Antony Moynihan, 3rd Baron Moynihan", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bridget Prentice", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "British Olympic Association", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Company Director", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Conservative Party (UK)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Craig Reedie", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Elected Hereditary Peer", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Hereditary peer", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "House of Lords", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "House of Lords Act 1999", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Incumbent", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Lewisham East (UK Parliament constituency)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "List of excepted hereditary peers", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Lord Temporal", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Margaret Thatcher", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of the House of Lords", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Minister for Sport (United Kingdom)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0,